Ben,

Sweet! I also made my first ascension today, and so I know how good it 
feels to finally win one. Woohoo!

PS - if you need another wish from a discharged WoW, you can always keep 
zapping it. You have a 1 in 121 chance of getting a wish per zap, so if 
you are in a nice quiet spot and can afford to keep zapping you'll 
eventually get your wish.

Jack

Benjamin Schieder wrote:

> Good Evening rgrn!
>
> Today, I'm happy to present you another busy seet in the demigod bar!
> And here is he, please welcome her with a hearty applause!
>
>
> Thanks, thanks, thank you very much!
> Yes, today, after around five years of learning - mostly the hard way 
> - I finally ascended my first character at nethack!
> Actually, it is what most people consider the easiest class, a lawful 
> human valkyrie.
>
> Blindcoder the Stripling    St:18/05 Dx:12 Co:12 In:9 Wi:10 Ch:9  
> Lawful S:70
> Dlvl:1  $:30 HP:14(16) Pw:2(2) AC:6  Xp:1/10 T:348
>
>
> As usual, I went down to do Sokoban first thing after reaching XL 10 
> and successfully dipping for Excalibur. Reaching that proved quite 
> difficult as the level below Sokoban has immediately the Big Room (the 
> X shaped one).  Nevertheless I managed and to my great dismay got a 
> BoH there. Well, it wasn't as if I hadn't already gotten one lying 
> around in the dungeon before that. I put it into my stash on level 6 
> to not accidentally blow them both up.
>
> Okay, after Sokoban it was time to visit the Gnomish Mines. Nothing 
> particularly intriguing happened until I reached Minetown when 
> everything changed. No less than three magic lamps where to be bought 
> from Izchak and a hardware store! Okay then, back to the stash, making 
> some holy water and wishing for the usual suspects: GDSM, GoP and 
> keeping the third for light and emergencies.
> Okay, equipped like that I made for mine's end, taking every 
> precaution available since the RNG must be high on my heels when 
> giving me something like this.
>
> Mines End was the haunted library and easily conquered.
> Travelling on I eventually encountered a neutral altar in the dungeons 
> and bought my naked AC down to 0.
> Along the way I picked up some other nice stuff that you just have to 
> have: Speed Boots, water-walking boots, a ring of free action and 
> others that were sink-identified and a few amulets. Using a few 
> blessed scrolls of identify (written with the blessed magic marker I 
> bought, along with the uncursed and cursed ones I found) I identified 
> one amulet as an amulet of life-saving.
> Unfortunately, there was no reflection to be found other than a silver 
> shield from an armor shop. Okay, bought that and when I reached XL 14 
> by wraith-baiting (okay, 15, had one corpse in abundance) I started to 
> travel to the quest. I easily reached Surtur by first fireproofing 
> aforementioned water-walking boots. This easiness made me a bit too 
> confident and I blew up my amulet of lifesaving by standing too close 
> to one of the drawbridges when a fire giant zapped a wand of striking 
> my way. YUCK!
> Surtur quickly fell to my wrath with a boulder standing on the upstairs.
>
> Then I discovered something extremely odd: a maze level above the 
> Valley of the Dead. Something extremely fishy was going on and then I 
> realized: BONES!  Unfortunately, there was only one usable thing in 
> there: a quite nicely enchanted elven cloak. The one dozen wands of 
> digging and another dozen wands of fire that also have been in there 
> were quickly put into my stash and I traveled on.
>
> Somewhere around here I blew up my silver shield somehow. IIRC by 
> (stupidly) reading an un-identified scroll which quickly identified 
> itself as a screll of destroy armor. Okay, here goes the last magic 
> lamp for an amulet of reflection.
>
> Came upon some barracks later which yielded a nice silver saber to me. 
> Collecting all the food (>100 C and K rations) I travelled back to my 
> stash, enchanting the saber and doing general changes here and there.
>
> Medusa posed no threat (was the small island in the middle of the map) 
> and quickly fell to my #twoweaponing. Having found a tinning kit 
> earlier I gave the tin of Lord Surtur meat some female (if ugly) company.
>
> Directly after Medusa came the castle. Here I camped for a few weeks 
> for the winter and new year's holiday :)
>
> Still being cautios, I read one of Sokobans scrolls of Earth in front 
> of the drawbridge so I could fill up one of the water tiles. Burning 
> Elbereth into the floor and dropping something on it I could easily 
> retreat to regenerate hitpoints. It wasn't needed :)
>
> I quickly emptyed the castle, extincting Soldiers on the way, and got 
> my hands on a shiny, unused Wand of Wishing (0:3). I didn't really 
> know what to wish for so I just wished up two blessed scrolls of 
> charging and a magic marker to write some enchant armor and weapon.
>
> Since I was quite low on potions to water down I decided to find and 
> loot Fort Ludios around here. Yielded some potions of full healing.
>
> Down through the Valley and into Gehennom I went. I didn't find 
> anything interesting here anymore so at some point I thought, maybe I 
> should equip myself with a nice T-Shirt and recharge the wand. Said, 
> done. Had a nice blessed fireproof +2 T-Shirt and a 1:3 WoW. Nevermind 
> the fact that I found a T-Shirt no 5 minutes later and another a level 
> below.
>
> Somewhere around here I found Grimtooth lying near a just-killed fire 
> giant and decided to take it with me.
>
> Alright, took care of Vlad, attached seven candles and searched the 
> square.  Found it, dug out an arrow of holes to point to it and went 
> on to Rodney, getting more careful by the minute.
>
> Came upon the first island and walked over the water just to find that 
> the plus-shaped building was already dug out partially! Haven't found 
> an answer to this mystery yet. I didn't do it and I haven't found an 
> indicator of bones on the whole level.
> Anyway, stepped through the portal, walked through Rodneys tower and 
> introduced him to Orcus... ehm... my wand of death (0:6).
>
> Okay, back down, to the square, lit the candelabrum, rang the bell and 
> read the book. Down to the Sanctum, swiftly killing anything in sight. 
> Found the door had the high priest in line, zapped my wand of death 
> (0:5) at him and stared at the words "You murderer." for about a 
> minute. anyway, took the Amulet, #name'd it and ran like the devil was 
> trying to catch me. Not that that was far from reality :)
>
> Had the mysterious force drag me down from Dlvl 39 to 41 but that was 
> it.  Some monsters appearing here and there which I just ran around 
> and Rodney reappearing twice. Wand of Death now down to 0:3.
>
> Standing on the steps to the planes I realized that the spell I 
> learned in Gehennom hasn't timed out yet. No reliable source of 
> confusion. Okay, had some potions I don't need (gain level, uncursed 
> water and others). Emptied a wand of polymorph on them to no avail. 
> Used my trusty WoW (1:3) to wish for two uncursed potions of confusion 
> and stepped up onto the plane of earth.  Introduced Rodney to my wand 
> of Death (again), confused myself and read one of the scrolls of gold 
> detection to find the portal. Far left side. Okay, ready the two wands 
> of digging and go. That went smooth.
>
> Air plane. Same as Earth, confusion, gold detection, portal on the far 
> right and made a run for it.
>
> Plane of Fire. This was my first visit here. Put on my lava-walking 
> boots and ring of levitation for double security. wielded the amulet 
> and tried finding the portal this way to no avail. after ten minutes I 
> lost my patience, wished for two potions of confusion (got only one) 
> and found the portal which I quickly jumped into.
>
> Plane of Water. With only one wish left (which I really wanted to save 
> for Astral) I wielded the Amulet and waited. 5 Minutes later it was 
> hot and I accidentally walked into the portal.
>
> Astral Plane. Wow. Now that I really arrived here I stopped to think 
> about what I've read about this mysterious place. First, I switched 
> off showexp and time to see more status about me. I readied my +5 
> Excalibur and +6 silver saber and started to head off to the left 
> altar. Got blinded by a potion and saw that Famine was waiting for me 
> there. Took 2 of the ridiculous amount of 60 C-Rations and three 
> potions of full healing out of my bag and fought my
> way through.
> When Famine suddenly came through the door I had the great idea of 
> stoning him (her? it?) with a wished-for cockatrice corpse. Well, 
> stoning resistant.  Okay, a few hits later Famine lay dead on the 
> ground and I continued creating statues of Priests, Angels and Archons.
> The left altar proved to be lawful. LUCKY!
>
> I quickly #offer'ed the amulet and was bathed in radiance!
